# The Findable Candidate — source-path rewrites
#
# INVARIANT 3 — every rule below MUST use status 200, never 301.
# 200 is a rewrite: the URL stays /li, and the page reads location.pathname to
# tag the traffic source. A 301 rewrites the URL to /index.html and every lead
# reports source: direct, destroying the only measurement the link scheme exists
# for. scripts/preflight.mjs fails the build if a 30x appears here.
#
# The page's own map (findability-checklist source, SOURCE resolver):
#   check → video · li → linkedin · tt → tiktok · fb → facebook
#   ig → instagram · yt → youtube · checklist → written · shared → peer-share
#
# / is served by site/index.html directly and needs no rule.

/check      /index.html   200
/li         /index.html   200
/tt         /index.html   200
/fb         /index.html   200
/ig         /index.html   200
/yt         /index.html   200
/checklist  /index.html   200
/shared     /index.html   200

# Real directories — no rules needed, listed here so nobody "tidies" them in:
#   /file  /intake  /privacy  /terms

# Lead magnet — added 26 Aug 2026.
# 200 like everything else here: the URL stays /playbook, which is what gets
# spoken on video and printed in RRL 1's welcome email. The PDF underneath can
# be re-cut and redeployed without touching a live email workflow.
/playbook   /assets/linkedin-visibility-playbook-for-jobseekers.pdf   200
